{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי תבוא בכרם רעך", :translit "ki tavo b'charmah ra'ekha", :gloss "when you come into your fellow's vineyard"} {:he "לנדר", :translit "lin'dor", :gloss "to take a vow"} {:he "סחור סחור לכרמא לא תקרב", :translit "sachor sachor l'charma lo tikrav", :gloss "go around, go around — do not approach the vineyard"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Order reversal: Scripture places 'vineyard' before 'field,' contrary to normal sequence, signaling the nazirite-vow warning."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'go around, go around — do not approach the vineyard' is a well-known line from a piyyut for Shabbat Zachor, drawing its imagery from the nazirite prohibition against vine products (Numbers 6:3-4) and the warning in Proverbs 4:15 to avoid the path of evil. The Talmud discusses how a nazir is barred not only from wine but from all grape derivatives and even from entering a vineyard (Nazir 34b). Ba'al HaTurim reads the unusual word order — vineyard listed before field — as an allusion to the nazirite warning.", :sources ["Numbers 6:3-4" "Proverbs 4:15" "Nazir 34b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא תתן", :translit "lo titen", :gloss "you shall not give"} {:he "כי תבא בקמת רעך", :translit "ki tavo b'kommat ra'ekha", :gloss "when you come into your fellow's standing grain"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Extended reading: 'you shall not give' (the sickle to your fellow) is pushed further — not even into your own mouth from a different species."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'lo titen' ('you shall not give') appears in Deuteronomy 23:25 in the context of not putting a sickle to another's grain. Midrashic and halakhic sources discuss how the worker's right to eat applies specifically to the crop being worked (Deuteronomy 23:25-26). Ba'al HaTurim extends the prohibition: one working in a given species may not eat of another species, reading 'you shall not give' as 'you shall not put [even into your mouth].'", :sources ["Deuteronomy 23:25-26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Order reversal: Scripture places 'vineyard' before 'field,' contrary to normal sequence, signaling the nazirite-vow warning.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Extended reading: 'you shall not give' (the sickle to your fellow) is pushed further — not even into your own mouth from a different species.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:48.467507517Z", :model "glm-5.2"}